From dda2ec9e4fe9c15f4cfc27ba373d3f0ca5996ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:22:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chat): settle run state when a run ends while the socket
 is down

A reconnect is a new server-side socket: every session room membership is
gone. Runs started from this client re-subscribe themselves, but a session
watched through the resumed-run path does not, so a terminal event that
fires while the client is away (WebView backgrounded, network frozen) is
never delivered -- while the REST stall watchdog keeps refreshing the
transcript. The UI stayed in run state forever.

- api: announce every chat-run socket (re)connect (global listener,
  mirroring the existing peer-user-message registry).
- store: on reconnect, re-emit resume for every session still believed
  live, which rejoins its room and reconciles the run state; a session the
  server reports as idle settles locally (run state, streaming message,
  running tools, abort/compression state, unread mark).
- store: on returning to the foreground, no longer skip the recovery when
  the client thinks a run is live -- probe the run state only, so a genuine
  mid-stream run keeps its locally accumulated deltas.
---
 packages/client/src/api/studio/chat.ts    |  27 ++++
 packages/client/src/stores/hermes/chat.ts | 153 ++++++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 139 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)

